{"id":49,"story_id":1811,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"Good. Would recommend it.","language_rating":"Good. Would recommend it. 1","created_at":"2017-04-26T02:38:46.922792000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-26T02:38:46.922792000Z","rating":4,"language_id":14,"comments":"1. Punctuation-spacing before the punctuation is uneven in most pages  ; check Page 9 where the inverted comma has slipped to the next line 2. Capital letters: Bow wow could have  uniformity in its presentation... preferably  with caps as on page 13 3. Language structure:The second sentence on page one reads a trifle clumsy: I would prefer garden not be repeated; suggest splitting it into two sentences – easier to read too"},
{"id":50,"story_id":1722,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"Good. Would recommend it.","language_rating":"Good. Would recommend it. 1","created_at":"2017-04-26T02:53:36.139183000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-26T02:53:36.139183000Z","rating":4,"language_id":14,"comments":"1.\tIllustrations: disparity as the cover has a princess with a western style outfit and teddy bear quite at odds with the image of the princess on page 4. In addition, the rest of the illustrations seem to have an Indian style.  Suggest -Change illustration on the cover to suit the rest of the book-seems more appropriate.\r\n2.\tPunctuation: most punctuation marks seem to have unnecessary spacing preceding them through the book. On page 6 inverted commas have moved to the following line. Moreover on page 10 inverted commas are missing before\" Will you..\r\n3.\tLanguage :Page 3 : replace the repeated \"in the forest\" with \"there\" . Page  9 Omit the first \"here\""},
{"id":51,"story_id":1890,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"It's alright.","language_rating":"It's alright. 1","created_at":"2017-04-26T05:12:10.580381000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-26T05:12:10.580381000Z","rating":3,"language_id":14,"comments":"interesting concept! Introduces kids to tales in verse. Also kids love scatological stories. However the verse and grammar on page  6 are clumsy. Also do not understand the need for  caps on page 7 for \"Terrified\""},
{"id":52,"story_id":1961,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"Good. Would recommend it.","language_rating":"Good. Would recommend it. 1","created_at":"2017-04-26T05:20:36.663017000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-26T05:20:36.663017000Z","rating":4,"language_id":14,"comments":"The illustrations seem to have problem ; page 1 is dark haired subsequently greyish hair...also in page 1 girl has two pigtails and then in subsequent pictures they all look like  boy with a girl's collar ...confusing to say the least !"},
{"id":53,"story_id":1974,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"It's alright.","language_rating":"It's alright. 1","created_at":"2017-04-26T05:26:41.861277000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-26T05:26:41.861277000Z","rating":3,"language_id":14,"comments":"Page 2:  “with” has to have capital letters “at” has to have capital letters\r\n‘Named it Tracy’ ..no need of ” as” \r\nPage 3 : I saw how all “the” pieces had fallen apart –sentence structure and insert word  \r\n“Breath” not ‘breadth’"},
{"id":54,"story_id":2001,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"Good. Would recommend it.","language_rating":"Good. Would recommend it. 1","created_at":"2017-04-26T05:31:00.752241000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-26T05:31:00.752241000Z","rating":4,"language_id":14,"comments":"Illustrations are good and idea at the end of sharing is excellent \r\n Grammar : Page 2 He WENT  closer to see what it was and FOUND"},
{"id":55,"story_id":1791,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"Good. Would recommend it.","language_rating":"Good. Would recommend it. 1","created_at":"2017-04-26T05:41:14.123410000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-26T05:41:14.123410000Z","rating":4,"language_id":14,"comments":"Page 2: Not “who” but  WHOM   \r\nPage 3: ‘Dida’ not ‘dida’ \r\nPage 5: Why the present tense of the verbs all of a sudden…  ARE = WERE THEN ;  ARE=WERE \r\nPage 6: The starry night SEEMS  to smile"},
{"id":56,"story_id":1902,"user_id":5834,"story_rating":"It's alright.","language_rating":"It's alright. 1","created_at":"2017-04-26T10:55:49.181257000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-26T10:55:49.181257000Z","rating":3,"language_id":6,"comments":null},
{"id":57,"story_id":1087,"user_id":5834,"story_rating":"Good. Would recommend it.","language_rating":"Good. Would recommend it. 1","created_at":"2017-04-26T11:01:38.681411000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-26T11:01:38.681411000Z","rating":4,"language_id":6,"comments":null},
{"id":58,"story_id":2093,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"Good. Would recommend it.","language_rating":"Good. Would recommend it. 1","created_at":"2017-04-26T23:56:55.731511000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-26T23:56:55.731511000Z","rating":4,"language_id":14,"comments":"1)Illustrations : Inconsistencies :on the cover Chinnu has straight black hair ; from Page 1 – page 5 brownish curly hair which seems appropriate ; From page 8 onwards the boy has a kind  of greyish straight  hair Suggest that hair is retained as brownish curly hair – at this level children do need  consistency in images  \r\nSecondly, the illustration for chocolates on page 5 looks very much like a box of Indian sweets unlike on page 3\r\n2) Recommended that the use of ‘&’ instead of ‘and’ is strictly avoided in children’s books \r\n3) Punctuation: The inverted commas are missing on Page 7 (before and after  “vegetables are your friends” ); Page 15 “Oh come … beans sambar”  ; Also on this page check the use of upper case \r\nPage 13 : No upper case  for “dear” \r\nPage 10:  spacing before full stop"},
{"id":59,"story_id":1933,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"Good. Would recommend it.","language_rating":"Good. Would recommend it. 1","created_at":"2017-04-27T00:11:29.652278000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-27T00:11:29.652278000Z","rating":4,"language_id":14,"comments":"1) Illustrations: Inconsistencies regarding the child’s hair \r\n2) The book has all verbs in bold except the verb “to be” pages 3, 5, 7\r\nPage 5: the verb “to hear” is not in bold and also suggested that “hear” be replaced by “heard”\r\nPage 8: The verb ‘have’ \r\n3) Structure: Page 5: ‘pretends he is fast asleep’ - Remove ‘as if’"},
{"id":60,"story_id":2057,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"Good. Would recommend it.","language_rating":"Good. Would recommend it. 1","created_at":"2017-04-27T00:36:31.013620000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-27T00:36:31.013620000Z","rating":4,"language_id":14,"comments":"The idea of the story is very good…teaches colours, days of the week and the concept of a rainbow.\r\nBut there are obvious mistakes and inconsistencies that absolutely need to be corrected!\r\nAlso check the political incorrectness of the idea that Kaalia is unhappy about his black colour …he could be unhappy about the plainness not so much the colour  OR  it could be a  dove unhappy about being plain white …. In the present context colour is a touchy subject \r\nSpelling:  VIOLET not as spelt on page \r\nType :  why is it that  page 3 and page 11  alone are not in italics ?\r\nPage 4: full stop missing after ‘colour’ and ‘kumkum ‘\r\nPage 6: full stop missing after ‘colour’ and ‘haldi ‘\r\nPage 7 :  why is “green zari sari” in BLUE font\r\nPage 7: full stop missing after ‘colour’ and ‘sari ‘\r\nPage 8 and Page 11: ‘u’ to be replaced with  YOU \r\nPunctuation:  indiscriminate use of upper case should be checked\r\nPage 8: full stop missing after ‘colour’ and ‘pavadai ‘\r\nPage 9: full stop missing after ‘colour’ and ‘ink ‘\r\nPage 10: full stop missing after ‘colour’ and ‘it ‘\r\nSentence Structure: “Everyday after lunch, they would put out leftover food for birds to eat” \r\nVocabulary: Remove ‘&’ and replace with ‘and’ \r\nContent : the days of week give you the colours of the rainbow in reverse red, orange, yellow green blue indigo violet EXCEPT  that orange and yellow have been interchanged \r\nConsistency and logic important at this level"},
{"id":61,"story_id":2138,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"It's alright.","language_rating":"It's alright. 1","created_at":"2017-04-27T00:49:47.788299000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-27T00:49:47.788299000Z","rating":3,"language_id":14,"comments":"The idea of the story is very good…teaches the concept of happiness but seems incomplete. The idea of 'seeing happiness only if one is happy' is too adult and will not be perceived at this age …or else there should be the idea of the unhappy frog that is happy when he sees Aloke… And what is the role of the dinosaur?\r\nLanguage is good but for a couple of errors  \r\nGrammar : Page 3: ‘Rain’ to be replaced with ‘rained’ \r\nPage 4 : remove ‘too’\r\nRemove ‘the’ before ‘nature’ ( 3 line from the bottom) \r\nPunctuation:  Page 3 removes inverted commas between face and Aloke (last line)"},
{"id":62,"story_id":1687,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"Good. Would recommend it.","language_rating":"Good. Would recommend it. 1","created_at":"2017-04-27T01:05:15.861938000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-27T01:05:15.861938000Z","rating":4,"language_id":14,"comments":"Very adult theme about death and love . Well written and engrossing tale with an ending full of irony but not quite certain the theme is quite appropriate and the children will certainly not understand the irony of \"you will be the death of me!\""},
{"id":63,"story_id":2198,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"Good. Would recommend it.","language_rating":"Good. Would recommend it. 1","created_at":"2017-04-27T01:11:32.625840000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-27T01:11:32.625840000Z","rating":3,"language_id":14,"comments":"While the level of  language is fine the sentences are breathlessly long and have no punctuation ...every page the sentence has to be broken up into two or several. It should be a second level story.\r\nPage 3 'himself' not 'him'; page 4 'yucky' maybe instead of 'yuck'"},
