{"id":70,"story_id":2083,"user_id":14254,"story_rating":"It's alright.","language_rating":"It's alright. 1","created_at":"2017-04-28T08:30:47.856038000Z","updated_at":"2017-04-28T08:30:47.856038000Z","rating":3,"language_id":14,"comments":"Good story, sound moral about being kind to animals … though only birds figure in this story. However text is marred by language errors.  Simple editing could give this story 4 stars. \r\nIllustrations : consistency in the representation of the boy required \r\nGrammar, Vocabulary and Punctuation:\r\nPage2:  They WOULD ruin his crops; ON sight; full stop missing at the end of the text \r\nPage 3: was quite THE OPPOSITE; THE farmer\r\nPage 4: slipped and fell (remove off ); walk ( remove for long)\r\nPage 5:  he was IN TROUBLE\r\nPage 8:  confusion between farmer and Father … resolve and use the same term throughout the text"},
